    <string name="rep_method_title">Method</string>
    <string name="rep_method_text">Each round records the Bluetooth state, the number of connected devices, whether CamAPS FX is present and the battery. That state is assumed to hold until the next round, for at most %1$s, and never past a phone restart; beyond that, time counts as “not monitored”. Link OK percentages are relative to monitored time. An outage is a run of rounds in the “no device”, “CamAPS silent or absent” or “Bluetooth off” state; its main cause is the state that lasted longest. Outages of %2$s or more are counted separately. “No BT device connected” cannot tell the sensor from other devices (watch, earbuds): a third-party device being connected can hide a sensor loss. History is kept %3$s days on the phone and never leaves it, except this report if you share it.</string>
